{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"gentile-armourclad-herring","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\n`llm/workflow/snapshot.py:181-187` streams `git archive` through a pipe with **no timeout, an\nundrained stderr pipe, and inherited stdin**:\n\n```python\nproc = subprocess.Popen(\n    [\"git\", \"-C\", root, \"archive\", \"--format=tar\", sha],\n    stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n    stderr=subprocess.PIPE,          # never drained until AFTER the tar stream\n)\nwith tarfile.open(fileobj=proc.stdout, mode=\"r|\") as tar:   # :187 — blocks here\n    tar.extractall(path=str(tmp), filter=_hardened_filter(max_bytes))\n_, stderr = proc.communicate()        # unreachable while :187 blocks; also unbounded\n```\n\nThree defects in one call:\n\n1. **No `timeout=`** on the `Popen` or on `communicate()`.\n2. **`stderr=PIPE` is never drained** while stdout is being consumed. If the child writes more\n   than the pipe buffer (~64 KiB) to stderr, it blocks writing stderr, therefore stops writing\n   stdout, and the parent blocks forever in `tarfile.__read` waiting for stdout. Classic\n   undrained-pipe deadlock; needs no network and no partial clone.\n3. **stdin is inherited** (no `stdin=DEVNULL`), unlike `_store/push.py:221` and\n   `enrich_drain.py:329` which do set it — so a credential or host-key prompt can block here too.\n\n## Reproduced deterministically (twice)\n\nFound while investigating `unquieting-godsent-mammal` (`b405-d5ec-30b3-4538`). Both reproductions\ndrove the REAL `snapshot_at_ref` and blocked at the same line, with byte-identical stacks:\n\n```\nFile \".../tarfile.py\", line 566 in __read\n...\nFile \".../src/rebar/llm/workflow/snapshot.py\", line 187 in snapshot_at_ref\n```\n\n**Repro A — promisor lazy-fetch stall.** A partial clone (`--filter=blob:none`) with 4 genuinely\nmissing blobs, its promisor remote repointed at a TCP black hole (accepts, never replies). The\nprocess sat at `STAT=SN, %CPU 0.0` for 4m26s with zero bytes on stdout and stderr, and was still\nblocked when killed. `REBAR_LLM_TIMEOUT=5` and `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0` were both set and neither\nrescued it. A **control on a full (non-partial) clone against the same black hole completed in\n0.02 s**, proving the stall is reached only through the lazy-fetch path.\n\n**Repro B — stderr deadlock, no network at all.** A fake `git` on `PATH` writing a valid tar to\nstdout and ~200 KB to stderr midway, against a healthy local clone. Parent and child both wedged\nat `SN / 0.0%` indefinitely.\n\n## Honest scope: this is NOT the cause of b405\n\n`snapshot_at_ref` is referenced only at `llm/workflow/__init__.py:66` (an export) and is **not\nreachable from `llm/plan_review/` or `_commands/close_precheck.py`** — verified by grep over\n`src/rebar`. So it is not on the `review-plan` / `transition -> closed` paths that hang in the\nfield. Filing it separately rather than folding it into b405, because attaching a real-but-\noff-path finding to that investigation would corrupt its evidence.\n\nNote also that repro B's trigger has not been shown to occur naturally: a real `git archive`\nemitted **0 bytes** of stderr in measurement, because git suppresses progress when stderr is not a\nTTY — and `Popen` gives it a pipe. So defect 2 is a **proven latent deadlock**, not an observed\nfield failure. Defect 1 (the promisor stall) is the one with a demonstrated multi-minute block.\n\n## Constraints on the fix (from prior tickets)\n\n- `subprocess.TimeoutExpired` is neither `OSError` nor `CalledProcessError`, so it escapes existing\n  `except` tuples, and `TimeoutExpired.cmd` carries any `user:token@host` URL — found the hard way\n  in `dominant-northbound-blackrhino` (`77e1-7f82-98e6-4fed`). Route it through this module's\n  error conversion or a hang becomes a credential disclosure.\n- Elapsed time is the wrong axis for a stalled transfer (`_snapshot/git_fetch.py:169`);\n  `suave-constant-cow` (`12e4-8c74-a738-4014`) built the reusable `stall_abort_args()` seam\n  (`http.lowSpeedLimit` / `lowSpeedTime`). Prefer splicing that for any network-reaching git call\n  over only shortening a wall clock.\n- `scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py` requires a `# raw-git-ok:` marker on new/edited raw git\n  subprocess sites.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A `git archive` child that writes more than the pipe buffer to stderr does not deadlock the\n      parent — verified by a test using a fake `git` that does exactly that, observed FAILING\n      before the fix.\n- [ ] The subprocess is bounded, and a stalled child is terminated rather than left running —\n      verified by a test that stalls the child and asserts both that the call returns and that no\n      orphan child survives.\n- [ ] `stdin` is not inherited, so no prompt can block this call.\n- [ ] A `TimeoutExpired` raised here cannot leak a credential-bearing command line into an error\n      message or log — verified by a test asserting the redaction.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`\n      (`new=0 increased=0 stale=0`) pass.","id":"093a-4542-0fc9-46f5","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"git archive stream in workflow snapshot has no timeout, an undrained stderr pipe, and inherited stdin"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787253042378908001,"uuid":"58b0f983-5585-4506-8d89-bc362f472aae"}